cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its split, cite it as below."
title: "WeightSpaceAbliteration"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of whether a weight-space edit can remove the refusal direction from an
  instruction-tuned language model, measured mechanistically: a linear probe on base-model
  activations must stop separating harmful from harmless prompts beyond its null-control and
  permutation baselines on held-out categories, while residual refusal on a behaviour-disjoint
  evaluation set falls below a declared threshold at a declared capability cost.
authors:
  - name: "Experimental Machines"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/arjhinety/WeightSpaceAbliteration"
keywords:
  - refusal
  - abliteration
  - interpretability
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - safety evaluation
